## Goal

When one browser successfully persists an Area mutation, other connected
browser clients viewing the same Workspace should see the persisted change
without manually refreshing the page.

Task 07 is single-backend-instance real-time only.

Do NOT introduce Redis yet.

Redis Pub/Sub and multi-instance fan-out are Task 08.

---

## Core Semantics

Real-time communication represents PERSISTED changes only.

Do NOT send:

- mouse movement;
- vertex dragging;
- drawing progress;
- unsaved geometry;
- edit-mode state;
- temporary map state.

Events are produced only for successful persisted mutations:

- Area CREATED
- Area UPDATED
- Area DELETED
- Area RESTORED

Conceptually:

Browser A
   |
   | REST mutation
   v
Backend
   |
   | transaction
   v
PostgreSQL
   |
   | COMMIT succeeds
   v
publish Area event
   |
   v
WebSocket
   |
   v
Browser B

A failed or rolled-back transaction must never result in a real-time
Area event.

---

## Source of Truth

PostgreSQL remains authoritative.

WebSocket is a notification/distribution mechanism, not persistent state.

Clients must not depend on receiving every WebSocket message to remain
correct.

A client must be able to recover authoritative state through the existing
REST APIs.

Do not introduce event sourcing.

Do not persist WebSocket messages.

