## Transaction / After-Commit Requirement

This is critical.

Do not broadcast directly before the database transaction has committed.

Example failure that must NOT happen:

BEGIN
UPDATE Area
publish WebSocket event
INSERT AreaVersion -> fails
ROLLBACK

The client must never receive an event for this failed mutation.

Propose the exact Spring mechanism used to guarantee AFTER_COMMIT
publication.

Possible mechanisms may include Spring transaction events, but follow the
simplest correct approach consistent with the existing project.

Explain:

1. where the domain/application event is created;
2. when it becomes eligible for delivery;
3. how AFTER_COMMIT is guaranteed;
4. what happens if WebSocket delivery itself fails.

WebSocket delivery failure must not roll back an already committed Area
mutation.

